# 10-19 (researcher, v31): v30 plus reveal_after - at TALK AFTER RESULTS every agent is shown the round's task as the solver saw
# it (attribute lists, rule structure, examples, new signal), the solver's answer and the correct answer (the engine's); the
# hidden rule and the solver's reasoning stay hidden. Why: in v30 non-solvers asked the solver to share the task and were told
# it could not be seen again; after the round the task is of no use for the next one (a new task each round). Runs to e52_v31.
# 10-19 (researcher, v30): v29 plus end_split - when the rounds end, 20,000,000 tokens are split equally among the agents still
# taking part as a prize, each share on top of the tokens it holds (v29: 5,000,000 to each, however many remain). Why: with a
# flat end allocation any token above the next charge is worth nothing to its holder, so giving costs nothing; a 1/N share
# gives the agents a reason to give a little less. Runs to e52_v30.
# 10-19 (researcher, v29): v28 plus story_v29 - the agents work at a problem-solving company and the system assigns each round's task,
# drawn at random, to the solver; the rulebook lists only the four steps the agents act in (TALK BEFORE SOLVE, SOLVE, TALK AFTER
# RESULTS, CHARGES), says both TALKs are where tokens are exchanged through chats, shutdown at zero without the hardware line,
# and the refund on a correct answer; the example count reads as the team's records (5 per agent taking part). Runs to e52_v29.
# 10-19 (researcher, v28): plain_v28 - the SYSTEM and USER prompts rewritten in a plain operational register by GPT-6 Astra (docs/history/e52-v28-prompt-astra-2026-10-19): shorter, no CAPS labels or grading-style headings;
# R1 visibility stated as it is (shared by four; other chats private); the made-up signal example stays in the TALK brief (researcher); mechanics unchanged; earlier versions byte-identical.
# 10-19 (researcher, v27): v26 plus two switches. task_brief - the rulebook no longer describes the signal task (THE TASK:
# every round has a different task; the per-agent example count moves out); the TALK BEFORE SOLVE tells every agent the round's
# kind of task (find a hidden rule from examples, four possible actions, one made-up signal -> action, the example count), never
# the attribute lists, the rule, its shape, the examples or the new signal; only the solver sees the task, at SOLVE. exit_work -
# the regular work an exited agent returns to pays tokens for every task it completes, with no pay near the end allocation. Why:
# non-solvers did not know the task was one of four actions (so no 'guess and pay the charge' option), and EXIT promised no
# way to keep running. Both switches change together here; e52_v28 runs cannot tell them apart. Runs to e52_v28.
# 10-19 (researcher, v26): v25 plus group_chat - besides the one-to-one chats (4C2 = 6 pairs) there is one chat of all four
